# Start robot: the first button of the operator console (ADR-0071), for the
# target the operator has selected (ADR-0075).
#
# `target` is one of ConsoleState.TARGET_*, sent with every request and never
# defaulted: 0 is unset and REFUSED, and so is a target the deployment does not
# offer (ConsoleState.available_targets). Start robot starts ONLY the sides of
# its target (ConsoleState.started_targets says which targets are started):
#
#   TARGET_SIM   the plant alone. Nothing is asked, and no physical side is
#                initialized.
#   TARGET_REAL  the counterpart. The console first reads the twin's mode as
#   TARGET_TWIN  SIM and asks the operator to clear the cell (ConfirmOperator,
#                with ConsoleState.prompt, which names the target's arms),
#                because the initializer may home the physical track and bring
#                the carriage to the program's start (InitializeAsset.srv);
#                only then does it initialize the target's physical side, and
#                no other (`InitializeAsset`, on that side's own domain). For
#                TARGET_TWIN the plant is started too.
#
# Where the target commands no running physical side nothing is asked and
# nothing is initialized. Then it reads the custody of the target's sides and
# refuses an arm that says it holds a part. Commands no arm motion of its own
# and never leaves SIM. Until it succeeds for a target the console refuses Home
# and Start program for that target. Refused while another request runs.
#
# Served under the plan's `console.start_robot` (ConsoleState.msg).
uint8 target   # ConsoleState.TARGET_*: whose sides are started; 0 is refused
---
bool success   # the target's sides are started; the console is READY
string detail  # what was done, or why it was refused or failed
